{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1376923-roll20-cod-sheets-pack","id":1376923,"title":"Roll20 CoD Sheets Pack!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-28T00:20:00-07:00","id":1376923,"title":"Roll20 CoD Sheets Pack!","content":"Because of COVID-19 quarantine, I needed to go online with my gaming - and as I started to use <b>Roll20</b> platform for that - I uncovered I cannot make all the PCs and NPCs types with official <b>CoD</b> sheets. So I started my own. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I made one very large sheet (pack) so that can you run any NPC in <b>CoD</b> universe with it, at least, in simpler terms. ( More to it in a moment. ) All the sheets are based on the <b>Mr Gone</b>'s sheets for various types I planned in original - and are to be used on tabletop (IRL) game sessions from here. My <b>Roll20</b> pack contains:<ul><li><b>Werewolf the Forsaken</b> 2E <b>Uratha sheet</b> ( as I run chronicle of it )</li> <li><b>Near-Human </b>( Wolf-Blooded, Ghoul, Proximi, etc. )</li> <li><b>Ephemeral Being </b>( Angel, Fae, Goetia, Ghosts, Spirits, etc. )</li> <li><b>CoD Rulebook <i>Horrors</i></b> ( like Hosts from <b>WtF</b> or Hobgoblins from <b>CtL</b> )</li> <li><b>Other Monsters </b>- Generalized sheet for Major Templates, like vampires, mages, changelings, prometheans, etc.</li> <li><b>NPC groups</b> - For lesser threats or secondary chronicle characters, like peripheral pack members in <b>WtF</b>.</li> </ul>All is based, for now, on <b>WtF</b> line, as I run game for it - but I would like to generalize as the product is finalized. Sheets are working, there are only some issues with CSS - and I cannot force it to show only one page at the time, not all of the subpages at once, as great conscious stream.<br /> <br /> If someone is interested in testing it, write private massages to me. Now in next posts will be screens how the Sheet Pack looks right now, in version 0.8.x","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T00:31:07-07:00","id":1376927,"title":"","content":"Sheet Pack, version 0.8 - Uratha page. Original sheet is from Kevin J. ( Rats ), I expanded and modified it.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/9MS9Yz2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachme